      "message": "Note: this get and subsequent set are non-atomic while later in this function (line 581), the atomic compareAndSetRebootEscrowErrorCode is used. I think this might be fine since the only competing thread is the network callback, which might set the error code to ERROR_NO_NETWORK after this get() but before the setRebootEscrowErrorCode() in lines 654 \u0026 566.\n\nAll that means is that the error code below will clobber the ERROR_NO_NETWORK error. Depending on whether this is a more \"important\" error, this could be fine. It\u0027s a question of whether you feel this will impact the quality of the error signals in metrics.",
